From f7070861e88a570266ea8e563e4b99b539ef5e1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:26:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] texts: this is not LibreELEC's build, and its media centre is
 not shown as Kodi

LibreELEC Hades is an unofficial build of LibreELEC, and a modified
build of Kodi that the XBMC Foundation has not approved.

Three texts of this add-on speak in the name of Team LibreELEC and send
the user to its forum for help with a build that it did not make: the
page "About", the end of the first-run wizard and the note of the safe
mode. They say now whose build this is, that Team LibreELEC and Team
Kodi do not make or support it, where help is, and where to support the
two projects. They are written in English and in Spanish. In a language
that this project cannot write, the translation of the old text gives
way to the English text: the first-run wizard reads the files by itself
and would show the old one.

The six texts that name the program that the user runs (the backup, the
two resets, waiting for the network before it starts) stay as LibreELEC
and its translators wrote them, and the name is exchanged where a text
is asked for (oe._): where it stands as a word of its own and does not
speak of Kodi itself, by the rule that the media centre has for its own
texts (utils/ProductName.h in the patches of Kodi). The texts that speak
of Kodi's own things keep the name: its log is still kodi.log.

The text of the setting for the internal disks that named the program
says "the media centre".
